# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first line is the one that matters. Both Dockerfiles do `COPY . .` in their build stage,
# so without this every `gcloud builds submit` uploaded .env — real Supabase service keys — to
# the Cloud Build source bucket and into an intermediate image layer. The RUNTIME images were
# never affected (they only copy .next/standalone and .next/static, which never contain .env),
# but the tarball and build cache were, and that is avoidable for one line.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never rebuild from a host install — the Dockerfiles run their own pnpm install / uv sync.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
.next
**/.next
.turbo

# Local state and artifacts that have no business in an image or an upload.
.git
.github
.claude
.playwright-mcp
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage
**/coverage
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Docs and design references — not needed to build, and a large share of the context.
# design/tokens.json is NOT excluded: tailwind.config.cjs requires it at build time.
docs
design/reference
*.md
!README.md
# Prompt artifacts are runtime inputs, not documentation — the proposer reads
# prompts/score_proposal.md from disk. Excluding them by the *.md rule would ship an engine
# that silently returns "prompt unavailable" for every score.
!**/prompts/*.md
